I fucked up the determinant thing again. Should be

lp__ <- lp__ - 0.5 * N * log(sigma_sq) + 0.5 * log(determinant(D - p * A));

with the multiplication by N. Also, if you do the second part of my original post, changing

    // model prediction
        log_mu <- log(E) + alpha0 + alpha1 * x + beta1_stz;
        mu <- exp(log_mu);
    // likelihood
        O ~ poisson(mu);

to

    // model prediction
        log_mu <- log(E) + alpha0 + alpha1 * x + beta1_stz;

    // likelihood
        O ~ poisson_log(log_mu);

It will go much faster and with less risk of overflow.

Ben

