If I remember correctly, in HMC-BFGS the rank of the approximation will end up being ~ the number of samples used to construct the approximation.  That's actually just an upper bound as the rank can be much worse if the set of samples is degenerate (unlikely to happen exactly, but it is likely to be ill conditioned, particularly early in the sampling).

