On Friday, February 22, 2013 6:34:17 PM UTC-5, rubi wrote:
> Thanks a lot Ben,
>
> I assumed what you mean in the code is something like:
> sigmaS ~ beta(c,d) T[,mu - mu * mu];
>
> I couldn't understand from the examples in the manual if this syntax is legitimate or not, and neither from the compilation error message:
> no matches for function name="beta_cdf"
>     arg 0 type=real
>     arg 1 type=real
>     arg 2 type=real
> upper truncation not defined for specified arguments to beta
>
> So is my syntax wrong or is a truncated beta not possible?

I guess we hadn't implemented the incomplete beta function to do the CDF as of v1.1.1. It is implemented on GitHub now. In the meantime, I put an example of implementing the Kumaraswamy distribution at

https://groups.google.com/d/msg/stan-users/4gv3fNCqSNk/4dwmJj1YwbsJ

It has an easy CDF too. You would just need to do

lp__ <- lp__ - log1m(CDF);

where CDF is the Kumaraswamy CDF evaluated at mu * (1 - mu).

Ben

