Can you send the full model, and not just the model
block?

You almost certainly don't want to evaluate
the sampling statement for c and d a total
of G times:

 > for (g in 1:G){
 >   c ~ exponential(1);
 >   d ~ exponential(1);

That's equivalent to saying

   p(c) propto pow(Exponential(c|1), G)

What is c?

That error arises when the sampler can't move at all
from 100 different tries at random initialization.

It can sometimes come from values being too extreme
which can cause arithmetic issues.

- Bob

