Isn't this what I've done by doing the following in BUGS/JAGS:
a ~ dnorm(b, c)I(0,)
c <- pow(d, -2)
d ~ dunif(0, 100)

Which in STAN should be equal to:
a ~ normal(b,pow(pow(d, -2),-0.5))

In which case the powers cancel out and you're left with
a ~ normal(b, d)

Which is what I've done...?

