On Tuesday, February 26, 2013 12:27:20 AM UTC-5, rubi wrote:
> Thanks a lot again.
>
> These data are only a sample of my real data (attached in just case along with the wrapper R script that parses it and calls the stan model), however I'm not sure that adding pseudocounts to avoid 0 observations will help.

If the data have 0s (or 1s), then the plain beta distribution will always fail. But a normal distribution truncated to [0,1] will probably not work well either. There is some work on zero inflated beta models; for example see

http://arxiv.org/pdf/1103.2372.pdf

Ben

