If you fill in the other half of the triangular matrix as
Ben suggests, at least this problem should go away.  I
patched the code in our repository so it does this.

 >>> for(m in 1:M) {
 >>>     Sigma[m,m] <- square(sigma[m]) * Omega[m,m];
 >>>     for(n in (m+1):M) {
 >>>       Sigma[m,n] <- sigma[m] * sigma[n] * Omega[m,n];
 >>>       Sigma[n,m] <- Sigma[m,n];
 >>>     }
 >>> }

- Bob

